<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n64394" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μά̆γᾰδ-ις</span></b> , ἡ, gen.
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μαγάδιδος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ath.
					14.634c
				</span></i>
			; nom. pl. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μαγάδιδες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					238
				</span></i>
			 (anap.) codd. <i><span class="en">
				Ath.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Phillis
			</span></i> ap.<i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				14.636b
			</span></i>; also, dat. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μαγάδῑ</span> prob.
			in <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>An.</u>
				7.3.32
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Anaxandr.
				35
			</span></i>; acc. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μάγαδιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Alcm.
					91
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Anacr.
				18
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				4.61
			</span></i> (-<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῐν</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Diog.Ath.
				1.10
			</span></i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῑν</span> dub. in <i><span class="en">
				Anacr.
			</span></i> l.c.); nom. pl. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μαγάδεις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hsch.
				</span></i>
			:—<i>magadis</i>, an instrument with twenty
			strings arranged in octaves, Lydian acc. to <i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				14.634f
			</span></i>, but ascribed to the Thracians by <i><span class="en">
				Canthar.
				9
			</span></i>, and derived from Thrac. pr. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Μάγδις</span> by <i><span class="en">
				Duris
				28
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				J.
			</span></i>; played with the finger, <i><span class="en">
				Aristox.
				<u>Fr.Hist.</u>
				66
			</span></i>; 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πηκτίς</span>
			, ibid., <i><span class="en">
				Menaechm.
				4
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				J.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>a Lydian flute</i> or <i>flageolet</i>, producing a high and
			a low note together, Ion Trag. <i><span class="en">
				23
			</span></i> (cf. <i><span class="en">
				Aristarch.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				14.634d
			</span></i>), <i><span class="en">
				Anaxandr.
			</span></i> l.c., cf. <i><span class="en">
				Did.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				14.634e
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i> [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μᾰ</span>, but <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μᾱ</span>- <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				238
			</span></i> (anap.), nisi leg. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μᾰγαδῖδες</span>.]</div>
